<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9721" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντερεί-δω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set firmly against,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρὶ χεῖρ᾽ ἀντερείσαις</span>
			<i>clasping</i> hand in hand, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.37
			</span></i>; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκναμπτον Ἥρᾳ μένος ἀν[τ]ερείδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					6.87
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντέρειδε τοῖς Ἐρεχθείδαις δόρυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					702
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ξύλα [τῷ πύργῳ</span>]
				<i>set</i> wooden stays or props <i>against</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.2.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. βάσιν</span>
			<i>plant</i> it <i>firm,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1403
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθοι οἱ-οντες τὰς περιφερεῖς
				στέγας</span>
			<i>springers</i> of a vault, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>stand firm, resist pressure, offer resistance,</i> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείκω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.8.16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				10.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				45c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>MA</u>
				698b18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				76
			</span></i> bis; <i>exert counter-pressure,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέναρι ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὠθούμενον ἀ. ὅθεν ὠθεῖται</span>
			<i>offers resistance</i> in the direction from which the pressure
			comes, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mech.</u>
				858a26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.924d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				923e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>exert mutual pressure,</i> of contending politicians, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.51
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> (dub.); simply, <i>argue against,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.57
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
